From da32aaed117b3ab1b42e53e124ecfebe5ee277fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ynk <evils.ynk@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:10:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] arm64: dts: qcom: salami: enable PMK8550 RTC with sdam
 offset

Android never syncs the PMIC RTC to wall time, so it free-runs from
zero and boots with a bogus epoch.

On this device the SPMI ownership of the RTC peripheral rejects AP
writes (disallowed SPMI write to sid=0, addr=0x6146), so direct
allow-set-time writes are not possible.  Store the offset between the
free-running RTC and wall time in a sdam cell instead; the driver
updates it when userspace sets the clock and applies it on read.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-oneplus-salami.dts | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-oneplus-salami.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-oneplus-salami.dts
index 01e6e9b18743..f41846f7b9bb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-oneplus-salami.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550-oneplus-salami.dts
@@ -633,6 +633,18 @@ pmk8550_sleep_clk: sleep-clk-state {
     };
 };
 
+&pmk8550_sdam_2 {
+    rtc_offset: rtc-offset@bc {
+        reg = <0xbc 0x4>;
+    };
+};
+
+&pmk8550_rtc {
+    nvmem-cells = <&rtc_offset>;
+    nvmem-cell-names = "offset";
+    status = "okay";
+};
+
 &tlmm {
     bt_en_default: bt-en-default-state {
         bias-disable;
-- 
